7756	{"artifactId":"LLD-f1bf0fb3085c629c-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-f1bf0fb3085c629c-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-07T14:20:49.903Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design addresses all three root causes the ISSUE names: (1) the edit session refuses shell commands, (2) the prompt asks for the repo-wide sweep, which overruns the time cap, (3) runSubprocess SIGKILLs only the direct child. It also keeps the fix intent's limit that other sessions are not widened.","evidence":"ISSUE-f1bf0fb3085c629c rootCause lists exactly (1) runEditSession with `--permission-mode acceptEdits`, (2) the TEST_CMD sweep in the validate prompt, and (3) `child.kill('SIGKILL')` in runSubprocess. The LLD covers each one. For (1), the daemon runs the checks itself and the judge moves to the read-only runReviewSession. For (2), the validate prompts are rewritten without the sweep, and the task's test files run with their own time limits. For (3), every child gets its own process group, the group is killed on timeout, and the group is swept on 'exit'. runEditSession, complete and completeStructured keep their arguments, so no other session is widened. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-f1bf0fb3085c629c.json, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today validate calls provider.runEditSession(prompt, { cwd: repoPath }) with no timeoutMs. It parses the verdict from free text, and passed is whatever the session reports.","evidence":"validate.ts:155 `const response = await provider.runEditSession(prompt, { cwd: repoPath });`, then validate.ts:157 `parseVerdict(response.text)` and validate.ts:165 `const passed = (verdict as { passed?: unknown }).passed === true;`. The ValidateProvider interface at :33-35 exposes only runEditSession. [files: src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runSubprocess/spawnOnce spawn the CLI as an ordinary child (not detached), SIGKILL only that child on timeout, resolve on 'close' and report -9 on timeout. runReviewSession maps the -9 exit to ReviewSessionTimeoutError.","evidence":"cli-provider.ts:594 spawns with `{ stdio: ['pipe','pipe','pipe'], cwd }` and no detached option. :598 `child.kill('SIGKILL')`. :605-607 `child.on('close', ...) exitCode: timedOut ? -9 : ...`. runClaude throws `claude exited with ${out.exitCode}` (:449), and runReviewSession (:366) does `if (/exited with -9\\b/.test(msg)) throw new ReviewSessionTimeoutError(...)`. The validate prompt asks for TEST_CMD (render.ts:29, validate-task.md:22, standalone render.ts:214). [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/mcp/build-step/render.ts, src/prompts/build/validate-task.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The only test callers of the ValidateProvider seam (_setBuildValidateProviderForTests with a runEditSession fake) are build-step.test.ts and build-start.test.ts, so the list of change sites is complete.","evidence":"A grep for `_setBuildValidateProviderForTests|runEditSession` across src/ finds validate.ts, build-start.test.ts (:121-122, :381, :451), about 17 sites in build-step.test.ts (:244 through :1215), and one direct CliProvider.runEditSession call in cli-review-session.test.ts:205, which stays unchanged. There are no other production callers. One caveat for the build: every existing fake returns only `{ taskId, passed }`. Under the new shape check (a boolean passed, an array checks and a string reason), each fake must also return `checks` and `reason`, or it will hit unparseable-verdict. [files: src/mcp/build-step/__tests__/build-step.test.ts, src/mcp/build-step/__tests__/build-start.test.ts]","action":"When the fakes are migrated, make them return the full judge schema ({ taskId, passed, checks: [], scopeRespected, reason }), not just { taskId, passed }.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"resolveTaskTestFiles relies on plan test names that start with a '<base>.test.ts:' prefix, and existing plans use that convention.","evidence":"PLAN-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1.json has test names such as `\"notice.test.ts: 'makeNotice sorts and de-duplicates ...'\"` and `\"load.test.ts: '...'\"`. 45 PLAN artifacts contain a `name` with a `.test.ts` token. The design says outright that names without the leading prefix are unresolved and fail the verdict. [files: .insrc/artifacts/PLAN-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reviewer session that the validate judge will use is read-only: --tools Read,Grep,Glob, --allowedTools adds only the two insrc analyze tools, no permission mode, and codex runs under --sandbox read-only. runEditSession keeps its acceptEdits / --full-auto arguments.","evidence":"cli-provider.ts:100-108 claudeReviewSessionArgs returns `['--print','--output-format','json','--json-schema',..., '--tools', 'Read,Grep,Glob', '--allowedTools', [...read, 'mcp__insrc__insrc_analyze','mcp__insrc__insrc_analyze_step'], ...modelArgs]`. :112-113 codex uses `'--sandbox','read-only'`. runEditSession at :320 uses `['--print','--output-format','json','--permission-mode','acceptEdits', ...]` and at :327 `['exec','--json','--full-auto', ...]`. These match invariants c1/c4. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every acceptance criterion (ac1–ac5) maps to a test that would fail without the fix. That includes the process-group tests, which reach the non-exported runSubprocess through a CliProvider with a fake bin.","evidence":"runSubprocess and spawnOnce are module-private (cli-provider.ts:570, :585, no export). CliProviderOpts.binPath (:120-121) lets a test point the provider at a fake bin script, which is the design's stated fixture ('A fake bin script that starts a long-running grandchild'). Against today's code, the grandchild-gone and exit-0-with-background-holder tests would fail: the group is not killed, and 'close' waits for the pipes until the timer fires and reports -9. The ac1/ac5 build-step tests assert overwritten testsPassed/typecheckClean and passed:false on a failing typecheck, which today's code cannot produce. The verdict-session-failed test is listed in the test levels but not in the acceptance mapping. That is acceptable because it is not an acceptance criterion. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-07T14:20:49.903Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
